          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mry9zajwg48rx4ar",
          "message": {
            "text": "Freezing animations is a determinism control, not a cosmetic one.\n\nThe screenshot regression suite only works if two captures of an unchanged UI agree. A running CSS animation breaks that outright: the sidebar's \"Guided review…\" spinner was caught at a different rotation angle every run, so eight scenes carried a permanent few-pixel delta no baseline rotation could ever settle.\n\nThe churn is the lesser problem. The real cost is a noise floor — once a scene always differs by a handful of pixels, a genuine sub-pixel regression there is indistinguishable from the spinner, and the reviewer is trained to wave small scores through. docs/ground-truth-screenshots.md already warns that \"a small perceptual score is not proof of noise\"; this removes the thing that was manufacturing that noise.\n\nanimations: 'disabled' rewinds infinite animations to their first frame and fast-forwards finite ones, so the spinner lands on identical pixels every time. Same motivation as the fixed viewport and device scale factor a few lines up.\n\nMeasured: before, two consecutive captures of settings-general and notes-guided differed; after, two full 47-scene runs are 47/47 perceptually identical (46 byte-identical — Chromium's PNG encoder is not byte-deterministic, which is why the suite compares perceptually rather than by hash).\n\nProving that property needs two full capture runs, far too slow for a unit test, so a conventions test (0) pins the flag itself.",
            "markdown": "Freezing animations is a determinism control, not a cosmetic one.\n\nThe screenshot regression suite only works if two captures of an unchanged UI agree. A running CSS animation breaks that outright: the sidebar's \"Guided review…\" spinner was caught at a different rotation angle every run, so eight scenes carried a permanent few-pixel delta no baseline rotation could ever settle.\n\nThe churn is the lesser problem. The real cost is a **noise floor** — once a scene always differs by a handful of pixels, a genuine sub-pixel regression there is indistinguishable from the spinner, and the reviewer is trained to wave small scores through. `docs/ground-truth-screenshots.md` already warns that \"a small perceptual score is not proof of noise\"; this removes the thing that was manufacturing that noise.\n\n`animations: 'disabled'` rewinds infinite animations to their first frame and fast-forwards finite ones, so the spinner lands on identical pixels every time. Same motivation as the fixed viewport and device scale factor a few lines up.\n\nMeasured: before, two consecutive captures of `settings-general` and `notes-guided` differed; after, two full 47-scene runs are 47/47 perceptually identical (46 byte-identical — Chromium's PNG encoder is not byte-deterministic, which is why the suite compares perceptually rather than by hash).\n\nProving that property needs two full capture runs, far too slow for a unit test, so [a conventions test](0) pins the flag itself."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "scripts/ground-truth/capture-screenshots.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 124,
                  "endLine": 134,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "async function captureScene(scene: Scene, port: number, outDir: string): Promise<void> {\n  const base = `http://localhost:${String(port)}`;\n  const pngPath = join(outDir, `${scene.slug}.png`);\n  console.log(`\\n▸ ${scene.label}  (${scene.featureArea})  →  ${pngPath}`);\n\n  const dataDir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), `glassbox-gt-data-${scene.slug}-`));\n  const server = spawnGlassbox(scene, port, dataDir);\n  let browser: Browser | null = null;\n  try {\n    await waitForServer(base);\n    browser = await launchChromium();"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
